'' A DEFINITION HELD TO ITS DECLARATION: 25 errors on fbc-modern 1.20, fbc 1.10.1 and
'' fbc-modern's Linux build alike, on exactly these lines (2026-09-19). fbc asks the
'' result first (40), then the parameter count (1), then each parameter (58: its type,
'' const, array-ness or passing mode); a member is found by its signature, and one no
'' overload has is 158 -- a changed parameter, a cast's result, a constructor, a property
'' setter's value -- as is 'sub N.h2' against a namespace's overload set. Lines 58 to 79,
'' 118 to 127 and 132 are accepted by all three: a default or a name that differs, a
'' typedef, the implicit byref of a string or UDT, a new module-level overload, an indexed
'' getter beside a plain setter, any type against 'byref as any' (but not a byval one,
'' line 136). The previous tiko-lang accepted every line.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -fmax-errors 100 --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/definition-mismatch.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 25
